    "senderName": "NWS Eureka CA",
    "headline": "Winter Storm Watch issued November 16 at 8:37AM PST until November 19 at 1:00AM PST by NWS Eureka CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Heavy snow possible. Total snow accumulations between 8 and\n12 inches possible above 4000 ft, with 2 to 4 inches possible down\nto 3500 ft. Winds could gust as high as 45 mph at higher\nelevations.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Trinity.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday evening through late Wednesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult to impossible. Tire chains\nmay be necessary if travelling through mountain passes. Strong\nwinds could cause extensive damage to trees and power lines. Roads,\nand especially bridges and overpasses, will likely become slick and\nhazardous.",
    "instruction": "Monitor the latest forecasts for updates on this situation.",
    "response": "Prepare",
    "note": null,
