    "event": "High Wind Warning",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
    "headline": "High Wind Warning issued November 16 at 6:42AM AKST until November 17 at 9:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
    "description": "* WHAT...Southeast winds 45 to 55 mph with gusts up to 75 mph\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Pribilof Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From 3 AM to 9 AM AKST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High winds may move loose debris, damage property, and\ncause power outages. Travel will be difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Winds rapidly increase in strength Monday\nnight/early Tuesday morning and peak late Tuesday morning as a\nstrong low pressure system moves through the Bering. Winds shift\nwest-southwesterly by Wednesday morning, and strong westerly winds\npersist over the Pribilofs through midweek. A second peak in winds\noccurs Tuesday evening through Wednesday morning with winds\npotentially gusting to 60 to 70 mph. As a result of the long\nduration of westerly winds, wave heights of 20 to 30 ft within 15\nto 20 nautical miles of Saint Paul are expected through Thursday\nmorning.",
    "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind. Prepare for the possibility of widespread\npower outages. Use caution if you must drive.",
    "response": "Prepare",
    "note": null,
